{
 "title": "Geometry nodes 2: a city of buildings",
 "summary": "Extrude Mesh (faces, individual or not, offset), Instance on Points (a cube on every vertex of a Grid), a Group Input socket exposed in the modifier (Height), Combine XYZ, a Math divide to lift each building onto the ground, Random Value into the instances' Z scale for random heights, Index + Compare to pick faces, and Set Material with a window material: a Chebychev voronoi through a constant ramp mixing glass and black frames, the glass coloured per building by a noise on Object Info > Location. Beyond the tutorial: set-back rooftops (top faces picked by normal, extruded, scaled, extruded again).",
 "objects": [
  {
   "name": "City",
   "description": "the geometry-nodes city"
  }
 ],
 "expected_result": "A 7 x 7 block of glass towers of random heights, each a different colour with black window frames and a smaller block on its roof, on dark asphalt.",
